# Shepherd App Flow Document

## Onboarding and Sign-In/Sign-Up

When a brand-new user first opens Shepherd on their mobile device, they are greeted with a warm and engaging welcome screen that introduces the app’s concept and the nurturing journey of their lamb avatar. The first screen provides a brief overview of the app’s mission to help users engage with Bible reading, prayer, and reflection in a gamified environment. New users are then guided through an intuitive onboarding funnel where they are asked to name their lamb, indicate their denomination, choose a spiritual goal such as “Overcome Sin” or “Walk in the Light,” state their current level of spiritual experience, and set their frequency target for engaging with the app. The onboarding experience is designed to feel personal and spiritual while visually reflecting a friendly, Duolingo-inspired aesthetic with a twist of gentle spirituality. Once the user completes onboarding, they are prompted to create an account through Firebase authentication. Depending on preferences and platform, they can either continue with an anonymous sign-in, use Sign in with Apple on iOS, or opt for Google sign‐in on Android. There is also functionality for recovering a lost password if needed, ensuring that users are not locked out of future spiritual engagement. The entire process flows seamlessly, ensuring that the user feels welcomed and fully prepared to take on their spiritual journey with Shepherd.

## Main Dashboard or Home Page

After a successful sign-in or account creation, the user is taken directly to the main dashboard, which acts as the central hub of the app. The home page is split into two prominent sections. The upper area features the playful lamb avatar on a scenic background that changes based on the user’s level of daily engagement and spiritual growth. This section also displays essential metrics such as the daily reading streak represented by a flame icon and XP indicators that keep track of their progress. In the lower part of the screen, three large and inviting buttons allow the user to either continue reading their Bible, start a guided prayer session, or engage with a reflection and journaling prompt. The navigation is straightforward and visually appealing, making it easy for users to jump from one activity to another while always keeping the overall spiritual theme and gamified feedback prominently visible.

